      "writtenOn": "2026-03-20T14:00:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Been doing some more digging today and giving some thought to how to best surface this. The goal continues to be to create separate Dawn objects for every pipeline (unless they\u0027re fully identical) but have some of them share VkPipeline objects.\n\nRight, I think there is a requirement to split the current [RenderPipeline] object into two pieces somehow. I\u0027ll just call them front and back.\n\nThe back object needs to own the VkPipeline, VkPipelineHandle and stuff associated with that like PipelineLayout. This is the expensive thing to create and it needs to be cached in a device level cache.\n\nThe front object is created for a wgpu::RenderPipeline. It would hold the dynamic state values for that specific wgpu::RenderPipeline. We could create one per wgpu::RenderPipeline without it being too expensive I think. When it\u0027s created it would lookup the appropriate back object in the object cache and if it doesn\u0027t exist create it (aka create VkPipeline).\n\nI guess the front object has to be the ApiObjectBase inherited class? That would give them separate labels which could be different as well.\n\nOf course this is just glossing over [all these member variables](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/RenderPipeline.h;l\u003d170-195;drc\u003d990c5fb665c34d2971c46728fcf22bff6e1b23290) and associated member functions that complicate things. Some of them are fixed and some can then change with dynamic state. That is about as much as I\u0027ve thought about the probem so far.",
      "parentUuid": "4766e0b5_13401a82",
